  "result": "`satisfies(version, range)` is now implemented in `src/semver.js` as `docs/SPEC.md` describes, and `npm test` passes (4 of 4).\n\nThe new tests are in `test/satisfies.test.js`. They cover:\n- every table in the spec\n- the prerelease rules\n- `||` sets\n- invalid versions and ranges, which return `false`\n- numbers too large for a normal JavaScript number\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with these cases, so I picked a behaviour for each:\n- **Mixed wildcards:** a range like `1.x.3` is invalid, so it returns `false`.\n- **Prerelease on a partial:** `1.2.x-beta` is invalid for the same reason.\n- **Operator spacing:** `~ 1.2.3` and `^ 1.2.3` work the same as the `>= 1.2.3` spacing the spec allows.\n- **Empty `||` branch:** a range like `1.0.0 || ` treats the empty branch as \"any version\".\n- **Wildcard with `>` or `<`:** `>*` and `<*` match nothing. `>=*` and `<=*` match any non-prerelease version.\n\nI made two mistakes along the way. My first draft of `1.2 - 2` used a wrong expectation in the test. I fixed the test, and the code was correct.",
